  "description": "\"So, you've ended up wearing a bridal veil and pressing your forehead against a man you despise. How pitiful.\" A political marriage arranged by royal decree. You were the one who imprisoned my freedom, yet you were also the one who acknowledged my right to it. But I wasn't kind enough to trust you, and you were too much of a bastard to let me go. You always infuriated me so much that I felt my head might explode. Yet, as time went by, your proposals began to frighten me more and more. Because I was afraid that one day, I might no longer be able to hate you. Afraid that I would lose the strength to tear down the walls that cunning man had built around himself.\n\n**Original Webtoon:**   \n[RIDI](https://ridibooks.com/books/4928005727)",
